[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6120719691","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124393#issuecomment-6120719691","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124393","id":6120719691,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABbNLFSw","user":{"login":"014-code","id":161032298,"node_id":"U_kgDOCZkoag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161032298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code","html_url":"https://github.com/014-code","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T08:38:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T08:38:00Z","body":"I traced this from the input symptom rather than treating it as a Control-specific issue.\r\n\r\nThe editor's GameViewDebugger sends `scene:runtime_node_select_setup` and `scene:runtime_node_select_set_node_type` when a debug session starts. On the runtime side, SceneDebugger forwards the node type to `RuntimeNodeSelect::_set_node_type()`. When the type is NODE_TYPE_2D, `_root_window_input()` disables normal input and sends mouse events to `CanvasItemManipulator::gui_input()`. The manipulator then calls CanvasItem editor methods such as `_edit_set_position()` and `_edit_set_rect()`. That is why dragging a slider moves the entire Control and displays the editor selection rectangle.\r\n\r\nThe important distinction is whether the game process is actually embedded. Embedded Game view launches the process with `--wid`, and `main.cpp` records that through `Engine::is_embedded_in_editor()`. Standalone desktop and web exports do not have that flag, even when they were launched from the editor.\r\n\r\nI kept the fix at the runtime boundary. RuntimeNodeSelect now starts in NODE_TYPE_NONE, and `_set_node_type()` forces that mode for non-embedded processes. Embedded Game view can still enable 2D or 3D node selection, while exported games never disable their input or enter CanvasItem manipulation.\r\n\r\nThe implementation is limited to `scene/debugger/runtime_node_select.h` and `scene/debugger/runtime_node_select.cpp`. `git diff --check` passed. All local-related tests have been passed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6120719691/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6127547520","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124393#issuecomment-6127547520","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124393","id":6127547520,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABbTr0gA","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Y